# How to publish a new blog post

No build step, no Node, no local setup required. Just:

1. Copy `_posts/2026-07-26-welcome-to-the-oasis-blog.md` as a template.
2. Create a new file in `_posts/` named `YYYY-MM-DD-your-title-slug.md` (the date in the filename controls the publish date and sort order — it must come first).
3. Fill in the front matter and write the body in Markdown:

   ```markdown
   ---
   title: "Your post title"
   tags: [release]
   ---

   Your first paragraph becomes the excerpt shown on /blog/ and in the
   homepage teaser, so make it count.

   ## A subheading

   Regular Markdown from here: **bold**, _italic_, lists, images, code
   blocks, links — all supported.
   ```
4. `git add`, `git commit`, `git push` to your default branch.

GitHub Pages rebuilds the whole site automatically (usually within a minute). The new post appears on `/blog/`, in the RSS feed, in the sitemap, and — once it's one of the 3 most recent — in the "From the blog" section on the homepage. Nothing else needs to be touched.

### Optional front matter
- `tags: [announcement]` — shown as the small label above the title. Use one main tag per post (`release`, `announcement`, `deep-dive`, `guide`...).

### Previewing locally (optional)
If you have Ruby installed:
```
bundle install
bundle exec jekyll serve
```
Then open `http://localhost:4000/OASIS/blog/`. Not required — you can also just push and check the live site.